### Security Guidelines

1. **Input Validation for Untrusted Data**: Ensure all user inputs are validated before processing. Use strict data types and enforce constraints such as length and format checks. For example, validate recipe titles and comments to ensure they are strings of a reasonable length and do not contain malicious content.
   ```javascript
   if (typeof title !== 'string' || title.length > 100) {
       return reply.status(400).send('Invalid title');
   }
   ```

2. **Use Parameterized Queries**: Prevent SQL injection by using parameterized queries for all database interactions. Avoid directly concatenating user inputs into SQL statements.
   ```javascript
   await db.run('INSERT INTO recipes (id, title, ingredients, instructions) VALUES (?, ?, ?, ?)', [id, title, JSON.stringify(ingredients), instructions]);
   ```

3. **Generic Error Handling**: Implement a global error handler to catch unexpected exceptions and return a generic error message to the client. Avoid exposing stack traces or internal error details.
   ```javascript
   app.setErrorHandler((error, request, reply) => {
       reply.status(500).send('An unexpected error occurred');
   });
   ```


